[about]
Title=01 - Install and Launch
Intro=The download, the installer's pages, the finish page and its boxes, and FileDir opening by itself.
Setup=The installer is downloaded, and your reader is running.
Homework=Install FileDir and open it from its desktop shortcut.

[step]

Say=The installer is downloaded; Enter opens it. Windows may first ask whether to run a file from the Internet; Alt plus R, Run, answers it.
Key=Enter
Hear=FileDir Setup dialog

[step]

Say=Each page of the installer is a dialog like any other: Tab through it, Enter for Next. The last page is the finish page, with boxes for what else to install -- the screen reader scripts, and mpv, which the Homer Player plays with.
Key=Enter
Hear=Next button

[step]

Say=A box that is ticked will be done; Spacebar changes it. Install means it is not there yet; Update, that a newer one is available; Reinstall, that it is there and current.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Enter on Finish, and FileDir opens by itself on a folder. The desktop shortcut's key, Alt plus Control plus F, opens it from anywhere after that, and brings it forward if it is open already.
Key=Enter
Hear=FileDir, List box

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I say the key; the reader says what it does.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus F.
Key=
Hear=Open FileDir
